From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 3ds-d2 <3ds-d2@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:56:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 3DS cache sync: the data cache by range through
 svcFlushProcessDataCache

Each newly translated block made the console clean and invalidate its
whole data cache (Luma3DS custom SVC 0x92) and invalidate its whole
instruction cache (0x94). The range variants were avoided because 0x93,
the instruction-cache range invalidate, faults on the RWX code pages.

The data side does not need the whole cache. The block is cleaned by
range with the kernel stock svcFlushProcessDataCache (0x54); the
instruction cache is still invalidated whole (0x94: an invalidate, with
nothing to write back). On a New 3DS a sync went from about 90 us to
about 25 us (ten sessions, about 22,000 syncs each), and it no longer
cleans and invalidates every line of every process, as 0x92 did through
the kernel range routine, entered past 0x54 own handler. 0x92 remains
as the fallback if 0x54 is refused, logged once to stderr.
---
 src/dynarec86/shim/ctr/mman_ctr.c | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 1 file changed, 23 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)
 mode change 100644 => 100755 src/dynarec86/shim/ctr/mman_ctr.c

diff --git a/src/dynarec86/shim/ctr/mman_ctr.c b/src/dynarec86/shim/ctr/mman_ctr.c
old mode 100644
new mode 100755
index aa9b406..890d03e
--- a/src/dynarec86/shim/ctr/mman_ctr.c
+++ b/src/dynarec86/shim/ctr/mman_ctr.c
@@ -262,8 +262,8 @@ static void svc_invalidate_entire_icache(void)
 
 /* Cache maintenance counters (always on: one increment and two tick reads
  * per newly translated block). A steady stream of these in play means the
- * guest keeps getting retranslated, and on hardware every one flushes the
- * whole L1 and L2. */
+ * guest keeps getting retranslated, and on hardware every one invalidates
+ * the whole instruction cache. */
 uint32_t dyn86_ctr_cache_syncs = 0;
 uint64_t dyn86_ctr_cache_sync_ticks = 0;
 
@@ -272,12 +272,27 @@ void dyn86_ctr_clear_cache(void* beg, void* end)
     dyn86_ctr_cache_syncs++;
     if (!is_emulator()) {
         const u64 t0 = svcGetSystemTick();
-        /* New 3DS (Luma3DS): the range variants fault in the kernel on code
-         * pages made RWX with MEMOP_PROT (data abort at the block's first
-         * address, DFSR 0x804: instruction-cache maintenance fault; Luma dump
-         * of 2026-10-17). The whole-cache ones need no translation. Their cost
-         * is paid once per newly translated block, not per executed one. */
-        svc_flush_entire_dcache();
+        /* New 3DS (Luma3DS): the instruction-cache range variant (0x93)
+         * faults in the kernel on code pages made RWX with MEMOP_PROT (data
+         * abort at the block's first address, DFSR 0x804: instruction-cache
+         * maintenance fault; Luma dump of 2026-10-17), so the instruction
+         * cache is invalidated whole (0x94: an invalidate, nothing to write
+         * back). The data cache is cleaned for the new block's range only,
+         * through the kernel's own svcFlushProcessDataCache (0x54): about
+         * 25 us a sync on the console, against about 90 us for Luma's
+         * whole-cache 0x92, which cleans and invalidates every line, other
+         * processes' included, and enters the kernel's range routine
+         * directly, past 0x54's own handler. 0x92 stays as the fallback
+         * should 0x54 refuse (logged once). The cost is paid once per newly
+         * translated block, not per executed one. */
+        u32 a = (u32)beg & ~31u, e = ((u32)end + 31u) & ~31u;
+        if (R_FAILED(svcFlushProcessDataCache(CUR_PROCESS_HANDLE, a, e - a))) {
+            static int said = 0;
+            if (!said++)
+                fprintf(stderr, "[mman] svcFlushProcessDataCache %08lx+%lx refused: whole data cache\n",
+                        (unsigned long)a, (unsigned long)(e - a));
+            svc_flush_entire_dcache();
+        }
         svc_invalidate_entire_icache();
         dyn86_ctr_cache_sync_ticks += svcGetSystemTick() - t0;
         return;
